{
  "_": "[SID:4542] the one definition of a tool's name a person reads (PO 2026-10-05 01:59Z · 02:04Z · Yuna 02:05Z · Kadir 02:04Z). Same bytes in sprintable-mobile contracts/tool-names.json (in the phone's own bundle) and sprintable backend/app/services/tool-names.json; both repos pin its sha256. Every vector: removing U+200B/U+2060 from *_wrapped gives the plain name, and the tool must match ^[A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{1,128}$ before it is named on a signing sheet (Kadir 02:07Z). Rules: (1) mcp__{server}__{tool} (any runtime) → the `mcp` words; (2) runtime claude → table.claude.names[tool] by exact own key (a value the daemon itself makes for a window with no tool of its own — story 4580 SandboxNetwork), else its own name as is; (3) other runtimes → table[runtime].names[tool] by exact own key, else table[runtime].other with {value} = the tool (a runtime not in the table: no names, codex's «other» wording); keys never matched by prototype or case. Wrap (display only, never signed): U+200B after _ - . / : (when a non-space follows) and between [a-z0-9] and [A-Z]; U+2060 between two Hangul syllables and between a Hangul syllable and an adjacent non-space non-Hangul character; nothing next to an existing U+200B/U+2060.",
